A RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation) retriever is the foundational architecture layer responsible for searching an external 
 knowledge base and fetching the most relevant data chunks to augment an LLM's prompt. While a basic vector store answers “which 
 text vectors are numerically closest to this query?”, a true retriever is optimized to answer the strategic question: “what 
 specific context should the LLM see to give the highest-quality answer?” 

Core Mechanics of RAG RetrievalThe pipeline relies on converting unstructured data into a structured search ecosystem before 
 a query is even executed:

